<urn:atm:triage:finding/QA-R2-001-AN11>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "QA-R2-001-AN11" ;
  triage:title "clippy::large_enum_variant on RequestEnvelope::Search after SearchRequest lifecycle field addition" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-core/src/protocol.rs line 49: RequestEnvelope::Search(SearchRequest) now triggers clippy::large_enum_variant under -D warnings (enum >=720 bytes vs 496-byte second-largest variant Receive(ReadQuery) at line 46). Regression introduced by this fix round: SearchRequest grew a new 'lifecycle: Option<WorkflowProjectionRequest>' field (crates/atm-core/src/search.rs:24-31), pushing the enum over clippy's size threshold. CI-corroborated: PR #874 Clippy check and all 3 Just-lint matrix jobs (macos/ubuntu/windows) fail identically. Recommended fix: box the variant (Search(Box<SearchRequest>)) at protocol.rs:49, check mirrored ResponseEnvelope::Search at protocol.rs:65 for the same issue, and update construction/match sites in crates/atm-core/src/api.rs, crates/atm-http-runtime/src/message_handler.rs, crates/atm-http-runtime/src/storage_and_nudge_router.rs." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-an" ;
  triage:triageMode "fix_round_2" ;
  triage:category "quality" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
